# Test: ze's machine reference is what it was before le gained its own help ai.
# accept-only: the registered native fixture runs the ze binary this run built,
# under the full feature set, and compares `ze help ai`, `ze help ai all` and
# `ze help ai --json` with their goldens byte for byte, services' env-var lines
# included. The goldens are per platform,
# internal/test/fixture/testdata/ze-help-ai-<form>-<GOOS>.golden, because ze
# links three linux-only plugins (iface-dhcp, iface-ra, memlock), so Linux
# lists three plugins darwin does not. A platform with no golden fails and
# names the file. To capture one, run `ze help ai`, `ze help ai all` and
# `ze help ai --json` from the ze this run built (runner.TestBuildTags) on that
# platform into the three files; a new or changed golden is judged by an
# independent ze-test-judge agent before it is committed.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-le-cli-usability AC-41, through the product binary and its
# real composition root.
# PREVENTS: the shared reference type or the help renderer changing ze's
# reference in passing.
option=timeout:value=120s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture ui/ze-help-ai-unchanged
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK
